CORE
default_disable2.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.0\.p0\] always main\.rst == 0: PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A 'default disable iff (expr)' (1800-2017 16.15) applies to all concurrent
assertions in the module, including procedural concurrent assertions inside
an always block (16.14.6). Here 'default disable iff (rst);' disables
'p0: assert property (rst == 0);' whenever rst holds, so p0 is PROVED.
Fixed in src/verilog/verilog_rtl.cpp: verilog_rtl_buildert::build_check
(which records assert/assume/cover statements inside always/initial blocks)
now applies default_disable_iff, matching build_property for module-level
assertions. The default disable is applied only to concurrent assertions
(ID_verilog_assert_property/assume_property/restrict_property/cover_property/
cover_sequence), not to immediate assertions, which are unaffected by
default disable iff.
